      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by \\(33\\), we start by identifying the smallest four-digit number, which is \\(1000\\). We then need to determine the smallest multiple of \\(33\\) that is greater than or equal to \\(1000\\).\n\nFirst, we divide \\(1000\\) by \\(33\\) and round up to the nearest whole number to find the smallest multiple of \\(33\\) that is greater than or equal to \\(1000\\).\n\n\\[\n1000 \\div 33 \\approx 30.303\n\\]\n\nRounding \\(30.303\\) up to the nearest whole number gives us \\(31\\). Therefore, the smallest multiple of \\(33\\) that is greater than or equal to \\(1000\\) is:\n\n\\[\n33 \\times 31 = 1023\n\\]\n\nThus, the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by \\(33\\) is \\(\\boxed{1023}\\).",
